; SGENT carries the deferred sequence break's flag into the stack group it
; enters, where SB-REINSTATE asks for the break again (sys/ucadr/
; uc-stack-groups.lisp; QUUX's Ethernet contract, section 2.6).  Load
; lisp/sg-deferred-entry.lisp first.  Each case defers a clock break inside a
; WITHOUT-INTERRUPTS and enters a stack group in one of D-SG-ENTER's resume
; states with scheduling allowed there: (BROKE VALUE), BROKE T when the
; scheduler ran a pass between the entry and the group's first form, VALUE
; the group's own result, intact.  With MIT's SGENT, which restored the
; entered group's own flag, BROKE is NIL in each.

; the pass counter runs
(sgd-start) => T
; awaiting initial call (SG-ENTER-CALL)
(sgd-initial) => (T 3)
; awaiting call (R-BIT)
(sgd-call) => (T AGAIN)
; awaiting return (QMDDR0): the caller, entered from inside its callee's section
(sgd-return) => (T RETURNED)
; resumable (R-BIT): a preempted process resumed by the scheduler, after the
; listener deferred a break and waited inside its section: two passes before
; the process's first form, one with MIT's SGENT
(sgd-resume) => (T 2)
(sgd-stop) => T
